+## firing what you actually hold
+
+A show is designed against the house catalog and fired from the magazine, and
+those two are never the same. Give any show command `--magazine book.csv` and
+every cue is drawn from stock in firing order: each cue takes its own effect
+while the lot lasts, and only once every cue has had its own turn does what is
+left over get covered by something else of the same calibre. A cue nothing can
+cover keeps what was written and the show is reported as not ready.
+
+`--pull vn2405,vn2413` sets lots aside before the draw, which is what a recall
+or a case dropped off the tail of the van amounts to. The book on disk is never
+written to, and the cue sheet grows a lot column so a shell can be traced back
+to its paperwork.
+
 A worked example lives in `examples/autumn`.
 
